<title>USA: US House member offers resolution on Boeing merger.</title>
<headline>US House member offers resolution on Boeing merger.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Congressman Jack Metcalf, a Washington State Republican, Thursday introduced a resolution that accuses the European Union of trying to seek unfair competitive advantage by opposing the proposed merger of the Boeing Co and McDonnell Douglas.</p>
<p>A spokesman for Metcalf said he hopes for a vote on the resolution when the House convenes Tuesday, one day before the European Commission is to vote on the merger.</p>
<p>The resolution expresses a &quot;sense of Congress&quot; that if the EU blocks the deal it would &quot;constitute an unwarranted and unprecedented interference in a United States business transaction.&quot;</p>
<p>The resolution also says that President Clinton should take &quot;such actions as he considers to be appropriate.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Washington newsroom, ((202-898-8300))</p>
